# UI styling

Read **`docs/03-usage.md`** when writing or reviewing JSX.

## className checklist

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<View className="bg-[#f6f6f6] rounded-[14px]">
<Text className="font-sans text-sm text-[#2563eb]">

// ✅ GOOD
<View className="bg-surface rounded-field">
<Text className="font-body text-body-sm text-accent">
```

## Common surfaces

| Use | Classes |
|---|---|
| Screen / sheet | `bg-canvas` |
| Input / OTP idle | `bg-surface rounded-field` |
| Input / OTP focused | `border border-foreground bg-canvas` |
| Error field | `border-destructive` |
| Links / actions | `text-accent` |
| Timers / hints | `text-muted` |
| Primary button (auth) | `bg-foreground text-white` via `AuthPrimaryButton` |

## Inputs (web)

- Whole field is tappable; focus styles on container, not inner ring
- Hidden OTP input: `caretHidden`, cells show digits
- Placeholder: use `usePlaceholderColor()` from `App.tsx` pattern

## Extending

New screen-specific spacing? Add token to `global.css` + `02-tokens.md`, then use `gap-*` / `p-*` utility — don't hardcode `gap-[9px]` unless migrating to a token.
